# Scribble Lab — Specification

## Scenario 1 — Room Setup & Lobby

### F1.1 Host Tracking
- When a player creates a room, they are automatically the host.
- The host is identified by `participantId` stored on the room.
- Only the host can start the game.

### F1.2 Room Creation Validation
- Creating a room with an empty or whitespace-only name returns a clear error message.
- Room codes are 4-character alphanumeric (auto-generated).
- Room codes are unique and collision-free.

### F1.3 Join Room Validation
- Joining a non-existent room code returns a clear error.
- Joining with an empty or whitespace-only name returns a clear error.
- Player names are trimmed before storing.

### F1.4 Room Isolation
- Each room operates independently. Participants in room A cannot see or affect room B.

### F1.5 Lobby Polling
- The lobby automatically polls `GET /rooms/:code` every ~2 seconds.
- The participant list updates without manual refresh.

### F1.6 Start Game Preconditions
- The "Start Game" button is only visible to the host.
- The "Start Game" button is disabled until at least 2 players are in the room.
- Starting the game calls `POST /rooms/:code/start` and transitions the room status.

### F1.7 Edge Cases
- Room code is uppercased consistently for lookup.
- Max participant limit is 10 (prevent unbounded growth).

### Acceptance Criteria (Scenario 1)
- [ ] Creator is host; only host sees "Start Game" button.
- [ ] Empty/whitespace name rejected on create and join.
- [ ] Invalid room code rejected with clear message.
- [ ] Lobby refreshes participant list every ~2s automatically.
- [ ] Start Game requires ≥2 players; hidden from non-host.
- [ ] Two rooms are fully isolated (different codes, different participants).

## Scenario 2 — Game Start & Drawer Flow

### F2.1 Start Game Transition
- `POST /rooms/:code/start` transitions room from `"lobby"` to `"playing"`.
- The first participant (by join order) is assigned as the drawer.
- A secret word is deterministically selected from `availableWords` (index-based).

### F2.2 Drawer Assignment
- The drawer is clearly identified on their own screen.
- Non-drawers are identified as guessers.

### F2.3 Word Visibility
- The secret word is visible ONLY to the drawer.
- Guessers see `"???"` or nothing in place of the word.

### F2.4 Player Name Validation
- Player names are trimmed on submission.
- Empty or whitespace-only names are rejected with a message.

### Acceptance Criteria (Scenario 2)
- [ ] Starting the game transitions room status and assigns a drawer.
- [ ] Drawer sees the secret word; guessers do not.
- [ ] First-joined participant is the drawer.
- [ ] Word is deterministic (same room always picks same word).

## Scenario 3 — Gameplay Interaction

### F3.1 Drawing Canvas
- The drawer sees an interactive `<canvas>` element.
- The drawer can draw freeform lines on the canvas (mouse/touch).
- A "Clear Canvas" button resets the canvas to blank.

### F3.2 Canvas Sync
- Drawing data is sent to the backend and retrieved by guessers via polling.
- Guessers see the drawer's canvas (read-only).

### F3.3 Guess Submission
- Guessers can type and submit text guesses.
- Guesses are trimmed and compared case-insensitively against the secret word.

### F3.4 Guess Validation
- Empty or whitespace-only guesses are rejected with a message.
- Correct guesses are scored 100 points.
- Incorrect guesses add 0 points.
- The drawer cannot submit guesses.

### F3.5 Guess History Sync
- All guesses (correct and incorrect) are visible to all players in the guess history.
- The guess history updates via polling.

### F3.6 Scoring
- All players start at 0 points.
- Correct guess: +100 points.
- Scores are synced to all players via polling.

### Acceptance Criteria (Scenario 3)
- [ ] Drawer can draw on canvas and clear it.
- [ ] Guessers see the drawing.
- [ ] Guesses are validated (trimmed, empty rejected, case-insensitive match).
- [ ] Correct guess scores 100; incorrect scores 0.
- [ ] Drawer cannot submit guesses.
- [ ] All players see the guess history update.

## Scenario 4 — Result, Restart & Final Validation

### F4.1 Round End
- When a guesser guesses correctly, the round ends.
- The secret word is revealed to all players.

### F4.2 Result State
- All players see:
  - The correct word
  - Final scores
  - Full guess history

### F4.3 Host Restart
- Only the host sees a "Restart" button on the result screen.
- Clicking restart calls `POST /rooms/:code/restart`.
- Restart returns all players to the lobby.
- Player list is preserved; all round state (canvas, guesses, scores) is cleared.

### F4.4 Multi-Room Cleanup
- Empty rooms (0 participants) are removed after restart if all players leave.

### Acceptance Criteria (Scenario 4)
- [ ] Correct word revealed after a correct guess.
- [ ] Final scores and guess history visible to all.
- [ ] Host can restart; non-host cannot.
- [ ] Restart preserves participants, clears round state, returns to lobby.
